{"type":"text","timestamp":1794050812519,"sessionID":"ses_e4a416acfffetoYUwsB6di0P2O","part":{"id":"prt_1b5c29f1e001uCCIhDAQluB1pa","messageID":"msg_1b5c25843001aJw1GwyCq2Wka7","sessionID":"ses_e4a416acfffetoYUwsB6di0P2O","type":"text","text":"\n\n## Objective\n- Implement `ledgerkit/limiter.py` with a thread-safe `TokenBucket(rate, capacity, clock=time.monotonic)` class and add tests in `tests/test_limiter.py` for a git worktree task.\n- Run `python3 -m pytest -q`, report the actual result, and commit the work on the current branch without pushing or switching branches.\n\n## Important Details\n- Working directory: `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e`.\n- Current branch: `crew/1107-8d1f9e`; initial commit: `92fe8b0 init`.\n- Required API:\n  - `TokenBucket(rate, capacity, clock=time.monotonic)`\n  - `try_acquire(n=1)` returns `True` and removes `n` tokens only if available; otherwise returns `False` and removes nothing.\n  - `wait_time(n=1)` returns seconds until `n` tokens would be available, `0` if available now, and removes nothing.\n  - `ValueError` for `rate <= 0`, `capacity <= 0`, `n <= 0`, or `n > capacity`.\n- Planned implementation constraints:\n  - Use `fractions.Fraction` for exact internal accounting to prevent cumulative floating-point drift.\n  - Use a single `threading.Lock` around clock read, refill, availability check, and debit.\n  - Bucket starts full; lazy refill is capped at capacity.\n  - If the clock goes backwards, do not add or remove tokens, set `_last_time = now`, and continue refill from the new time.\n  - `wait_time` must return an upward-rounded float; merely calling `float()` may round down.\n  - For `wait_time`, simulate the fake/real clock advance as `float(_last_time) + returned_delay`, then use `math.nextafter(..., math.inf)` until the exact simulated elapsed time is sufficient.\n  - Reject non-finite/non-numeric values; likely reject `bool` as not a real number.\n  - Tests should import `ledgerkit.limiter.TokenBucket`; do not export from `ledgerkit/__init__.py` unless required.\n- Test plan:\n  - Use a mutable `FakeClock` returning `self.t`.\n  - Cover starts full, correct debit, failed acquire leaves balance unchanged.\n  - Cover lazy refill only on method calls and cap at capacity.\n  - Cover `wait_time` zero when affordable, positive when not, and no token consumption.\n  - Parameterize invalid constructor arguments and invalid `n` for both methods, including `n > capacity`.\n  - Cover clock rollback with no token change and immediate refill from the new time.\n  - Numerical regression for rates `0.1`, `3`, and `7` over thousands of cycles: wait exactly `wait_time(n)` then `try_acquire(n)` must succeed.\n  - Thread-safety test with fixed fake clock: many threads requesting one token must total exactly `capacity` successes.\n- Environment facts:\n  - Python 3.12.3 available.\n  - `pytest 7.4.4` is available, so the baseline note that `pytest` is missing is outdated.\n  - Existing repo is minimal: empty `ledgerkit/__init__.py`, simple `ledgerkit/money.py`, `tests/test_money.py`, and `README.md` says tests run with `python3 -m pytest -q`.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Explored repository structure and confirmed existing files and conventions.\n- Verified `python3` and `pytest` are available.\n- Confirmed git worktree is on branch `crew/1107-8d1f9e` at commit `92fe8b0 init` and appears clean.\n- Formed detailed implementation and test plan for `TokenBucket` and `tests/test_limiter.py`.\n\n### Active\n- Ready to create `ledgerkit/limiter.py` implementing `TokenBucket` with exact `Fraction` accounting, locking, lazy refill, rollback handling, and validation.\n- Ready to create `tests/test_limiter.py` covering all required behavior and the numerical/threading regression tests.\n- No code files have been created or modified yet.\n\n### Blocked\n- None. `pytest` is installed despite the earlier baseline note.\n\n## Next Move\n1. Create `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/ledgerkit/limiter.py` with the planned `TokenBucket` implementation.\n2. Create `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/tests/test_limiter.py` with the planned test suite.\n3. Run `python3 -m pytest -q` from the worktree, record the actual result, fix failures if any, then commit to the current branch with a clear message.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/ledgerkit/limiter.py`: target new module to create.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/tests/test_limiter.py`: target new test file to create.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/ledgerkit/__init__.py`: currently empty; likely should remain unchanged.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/ledgerkit/money.py`: existing style reference; simple module with a short docstring.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/tests/test_money.py`: existing test style reference.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/README.md`: states tests should run with `python3 -m pytest -q`.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/.gitignore`: ignores `__pycache__/` and `.pytest_cache/`.","time":{"start":1794050793246,"end":1794050812495}}}
