{"type":"text","timestamp":1794051187315,"sessionID":"ses_e4a416acfffetoYUwsB6di0P2O","part":{"id":"prt_1b5c83e0d001Q1emAPdxZde2qT","messageID":"msg_1b5c7c24d0011tBG86b5NhGum4","sessionID":"ses_e4a416acfffetoYUwsB6di0P2O","type":"text","text":"\n\n## Objective\n- Implement a thread-safe `TokenBucket` rate limiter in `ledgerkit/limiter.py` with tests in `tests/test_limiter.py`, run `python3 -m pytest -q`, and commit the work on the current worktree branch.\n\n## Important Details\n- Working directory: `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e`.\n- Branch: `crew/1107-8d1f9e`; baseline commit: `92fe8b0 init`.\n- Required API:\n  - `TokenBucket(rate, capacity, clock=time.monotonic)`\n  - `try_acquire(n=1)` returns `True` and removes `n` tokens only if available; otherwise returns `False` and removes nothing.\n  - `wait_time(n=1)` returns seconds until `n` tokens would be available, `0.0` if available now, and never removes tokens.\n  - Raise `ValueError` for `rate <= 0`, `capacity <= 0`, `n <= 0`, or `n > capacity`.\n- Implementation decisions:\n  - Use `fractions.Fraction` for exact internal token accounting to avoid cumulative float drift.\n  - Use a single `threading.Lock` around validation, clock read, refill, availability check, and debit.\n  - Bucket starts full at construction.\n  - Refill is lazy: only computed when `try_acquire` or `wait_time` is called.\n  - Refill is capped at `capacity`.\n  - If the clock reports a time earlier than `_last_time`, do not add or remove tokens; set `_last_time = now` and continue from that time.\n  - `wait_time` must return an upward-rounded float so that advancing the clock by exactly that float makes the next `try_acquire(n)` succeed.\n  - `wait_time` simulation must mirror the exact float arithmetic used by tests and real refill:\n    - `simulated = float(self._last_time) + seconds`\n    - `delta = simulated - self._last_time`\n    - `gained = Fraction(delta) * self._rate if delta > 0 else Fraction(0)`\n  - Use `math.nextafter(seconds, math.inf)` to bump the candidate delay until the simulated refill is sufficient.\n  - Add an `OverflowError` guard if `float(deficit / self._rate)` is not finite.\n  - Reject `bool` explicitly; convert other numeric values via `Fraction`; translate `TypeError`/`ValueError` from `Fraction` into `ValueError`.\n  - Validate `n` before mutating/refilling in both methods.\n- Planned helper behavior:\n  - `_as_fraction(value, name)` rejects `bool`, non-numeric values, and non-finite values with `ValueError`.\n  - Constructor messages may be:\n    - `rate must be positive`\n    - `capacity must be positive`\n    - `rate must be a real number`\n    - `capacity must be a real number`\n  - `_checked_amount(n)` may raise:\n    - `n must be positive`\n    - `n exceeds the bucket capacity`\n- Test design decisions:\n  - Use `FakeClock` with mutable float `self.t` and `__call__` returning `self.t`.\n  - Tests should advance the clock exactly as: `clock.t = float(clock.t) + wait`.\n  - Corrected lazy-refill test: after draining capacity `2` with rate `1`, advancing to `t=1.0` and calling `wait_time(2)` should return `1.0`, not `wait_time(1)`, because `wait_time` itself triggers refill.\n  - Default-clock smoke test should not assert exact `1.0`, because real elapsed time is nonzero; use `0.0 < bucket.wait_time(1) < 2.0`.\n  - Include numerical regression over many cycles using rates `0.1`, `3`, `7` and amounts `1`, `3`, capacity `10`, 1000 cycles.\n  - Include thread-safety test: fixed fake clock, capacity `1000`, 20 threads × 60 attempts, total successful `try_acquire(1)` calls must equal exactly `1000`.\n- Existing repo style is minimal:\n  - `ledgerkit/money.py` defines `split(total_cents, weights)` with a short docstring.\n  - `tests/test_money.py` imports `ledgerkit.money.split` and has one simple test.\n- `ledgerkit/__init__.py` should remain unchanged/empty unless needed.\n- Environment facts:\n  - Python 3.12.3 is available.\n  - `pytest 7.4.4` is available.\n  - README expects tests to run with `python3 -m pytest -q`.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Explored repository structure and confirmed existing files and conventions.\n- Verified `python3` and `pytest` availability.\n- Confirmed worktree is on `crew/1107-8d1f9e` at `92fe8b0 init` and clean.\n- Read `ledgerkit/money.py` and `tests/test_money.py` for style reference.\n- Finalized implementation design for `TokenBucket`, including validation, exact `Fraction` accounting, rollback handling, and upward-rounded `wait_time` simulation.\n- Finalized test plan, including corrected lazy-refill assertion, numerical regression, threading test, and invalid-input tests.\n\n### Active\n- About to create `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/ledgerkit/limiter.py`.\n- About to create `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/tests/test_limiter.py`.\n- No code files have been created or modified yet.\n\n### Blocked\n- None.\n\n## Next Move\n1. Write `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/ledgerkit/limiter.py` implementing:\n   - module-level `_as_fraction(value, name)`\n   - `TokenBucket.__init__` with validation and full initial bucket\n   - `try_acquire(n=1)`\n   - `wait_time(n=1)`\n   - `_checked_amount(n)`\n   - `_refill()`\n2. Write `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/tests/test_limiter.py` with the planned `FakeClock` and full test suite.\n3. Run `python3 -m pytest -q` from `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e`, fix any failures, then commit the new files on the current branch.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/ledgerkit/limiter.py`: target new module for `TokenBucket`.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/tests/test_limiter.py`: target new test file.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/ledgerkit/__init__.py`: currently empty; likely unchanged.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/ledgerkit/money.py`: existing style reference.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/tests/test_money.py`: existing test style reference.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/README.md`: states tests should run with `python3 -m pytest -q`.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/.gitignore`: ignores `__pycache__/` and `.pytest_cache/`.","time":{"start":1794051161613,"end":1794051187311}}}
