{"type":"text","timestamp":1794051684864,"sessionID":"ses_e4a416acfffetoYUwsB6di0P2O","part":{"id":"prt_1b5cfd137001bCwQGIrg17l6n7","messageID":"msg_1b5cf96bf001oxZsz27Zje6NVn","sessionID":"ses_e4a416acfffetoYUwsB6di0P2O","type":"text","text":"\n\n## Objective\n- Implement a thread-safe `TokenBucket` rate limiter in `ledgerkit/limiter.py`, add tests in `tests/test_limiter.py`, run `python3 -m pytest -q`, and commit the new files on the current worktree branch.\n\n## Important Details\n- Working directory: `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e`.\n- Branch: `crew/1107-8d1f9e`; baseline commit: `92fe8b0 init`.\n- Required API:\n  - `TokenBucket(rate, capacity, clock=time.monotonic)`\n  - `try_acquire(n=1)` returns `True` and removes `n` tokens only if available; otherwise returns `False` and removes nothing.\n  - `wait_time(n=1)` returns seconds until `n` tokens would be available, `0.0` if available now, and never removes tokens.\n  - Raise `ValueError` for `rate <= 0`, `capacity <= 0`, `n <= 0`, or `n > capacity`.\n- `ledgerkit/limiter.py` has already been created with:\n  - module-level `_as_fraction(value, name)`\n  - `TokenBucket.__init__` with validation and full initial bucket\n  - `try_acquire(n=1)`\n  - `wait_time(n=1)`\n  - `_checked_amount(n)`\n  - `_refill()`\n- Implementation behavior in the created module:\n  - Uses `fractions.Fraction` for exact internal token accounting.\n  - Uses a single `threading.Lock` around validation, clock read, refill, availability check, and debit.\n  - Bucket starts full at construction.\n  - Refill is lazy and capped at `capacity`.\n  - If the clock reports a time earlier than `_last_time`, no tokens are added or removed; `_last_time` is set to the earlier time.\n  - `wait_time` returns an upward-rounded float so advancing the clock by exactly that float makes the next `try_acquire(n)` succeed.\n  - `wait_time` simulation mirrors refill arithmetic:\n    - `simulated = self._last_time + seconds`\n    - `delta = simulated - self._last_time`\n    - `gained = Fraction(delta) * self._rate if delta > 0 else Fraction(0)`\n  - Uses `math.nextafter(seconds, math.inf)` to bump the candidate delay until simulated refill is sufficient.\n  - Raises `OverflowError` if `float(deficit / self._rate)` overflows or simulated time becomes non-finite.\n  - `_as_fraction` rejects `bool`, `str`, `bytes`, `bytearray`, non-numeric values, and non-finite values with `ValueError`.\n  - Validation messages include:\n    - `rate must be positive`\n    - `capacity must be positive`\n    - `n must be positive`\n    - `n exceeds the bucket capacity`\n    - `rate must be a real number`\n    - `capacity must be a real number`\n- Test plan for `tests/test_limiter.py`:\n  - Use `FakeClock` with mutable float `self.t` and `__call__` returning `self.t`.\n  - Advance the clock exactly as: `clock.t = float(clock.t) + wait`.\n  - Include tests for:\n    - bucket starts full\n    - failed `try_acquire` does not partially consume\n    - refill over time\n    - refill capped at capacity\n    - `wait_time` does not consume tokens\n    - `wait_time` for missing tokens\n    - lazy refill before waiting, e.g. after draining capacity `2` with rate `1`, advancing to `t=1.0`, `wait_time(2)` returns `1.0`\n    - advancing by `wait_time` result makes `try_acquire` succeed\n    - many wait/acquire cycles do not drift\n    - thread safety with fixed fake clock, capacity `1000`, 20 threads × 60 attempts, exactly `1000` successful `try_acquire(1)` calls\n    - fractional rate/capacity\n    - clock going backward does not refill\n    - default clock smoke test using `0.0 < bucket.wait_time(1) < 2.0`\n    - invalid `rate`, `capacity`, and `n` values, including `0`, negative numbers, NaN, infinity, negative infinity, strings, booleans, `None`, lists, and dicts\n    - `n` exceeding capacity\n    - invalid `n` does not mutate bucket state\n- Existing repo style is minimal:\n  - `ledgerkit/money.py` defines `split(total_cents, weights)` with a short docstring.\n  - `tests/test_money.py` imports `ledgerkit.money.split` and has one simple test.\n- `ledgerkit/__init__.py` should remain unchanged/empty unless needed.\n- Environment facts:\n  - Python 3.12.3 is available.\n  - `pytest 7.4.4` is available.\n  - README expects tests to run with `python3 -m pytest -q`.\n- No existing limiter-related code or references were present before the newly created `ledgerkit/limiter.py`.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Explored repository structure and confirmed existing files and conventions.\n- Verified `python3` and `pytest` availability.\n- Confirmed worktree is on `crew/1107-8d1f9e` at `92fe8b0 init` and clean before implementation.\n- Read `ledgerkit/money.py` and `tests/test_money.py` for style reference.\n- Finalized implementation design for `TokenBucket`, including validation, exact `Fraction` accounting, rollback handling, and upward-rounded `wait_time` simulation.\n- Finalized test plan, including corrected lazy-refill assertion, numerical regression, threading test, invalid-input tests, and default-clock smoke test.\n- Created `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/ledgerkit/limiter.py` with the planned `TokenBucket` implementation.\n\n### Active\n- Need to create `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/tests/test_limiter.py` with the planned `FakeClock` and full test suite.\n- Need to run `python3 -m pytest -q` from `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e`, fix any failures, inspect Git state, stage only the new files, and commit.\n\n### Blocked\n- None.\n\n## Next Move\n1. Write `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/tests/test_limiter.py` implementing the planned `FakeClock` and full test suite.\n2. Run `python3 -m pytest -q` from `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e`, fix any failures, then inspect `git status --short`, `git diff`, and `git log --oneline -5`.\n3. Stage only `ledgerkit/limiter.py` and `tests/test_limiter.py`, and commit with a concise message such as `Add token bucket rate limiter`.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/ledgerkit/limiter.py`: newly created `TokenBucket` module; needs testing and commit.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/tests/test_limiter.py`: target new test file, not yet created.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/ledgerkit/__init__.py`: currently empty; likely unchanged.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/ledgerkit/money.py`: existing style reference.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/tests/test_money.py`: existing test style reference.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/README.md`: states tests should run with `python3 -m pytest -q`.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-8d1f9e/.gitignore`: ignores `__pycache__/` and `.pytest_cache/`.","time":{"start":1794051658039,"end":1794051684861}}}
